From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 22:30:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] constellation: Abort superseded iframe navigations

When an iframe is navigated again before the document of an earlier
navigation has been activated, close the earlier navigation's pending
pipeline. Previously both documents were activated in whatever order
their responses arrived. If the earlier one arrived last, it replaced
the newer document before that finished loading, while the iframe
element kept waiting for the newer one, so the iframe's load event never
fired and the parent document never finished loading.

Starting a navigation aborts earlier ongoing navigations of the same
navigable (step 20 of
https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/#navigate). History traversals
that reload an entry are not aborted.

iframe-loading-lazy-reload-location-reload.html no longer hangs but
fails: location.reload() reaches the iframe element after the lazy src
navigation, because it goes through the embedder's navigation approval
first, so the reload wins.

Fork note: meant for upstream, where it fixes upstream issue 29634 and
the CRASH ("Browser not responding") intermittents of seven other tests
that navigate one iframe twice. Same change as the upstream-bound
commit; drop it (decision 3) once upstream has landed it.

Testing: Adds a WPT test that times out without this change.

Validation: Release build of ohos-main plus this patch. `./mach test-wpt --release --processes 1 --repeat 10 html/browsers/browsing-the-web/overlapping-navigations-and-traversals/cross-document-nav-cross-document-nav-slow-first-response.html`: 10/10 PASS; `--repeat 25 html/semantics/forms/form-submission-0/form-submit-iframe-then-location-navigate.html`: 25/25 as expected, no hang; `--processes 2 --repeat 10` of assign-replace-from-iframe.html, security_location_0.htm, replace-with-nested-iframe.html, sandbox-initial-empty-document-toward-same-origin.html, iframe-loading-lazy-nav-location-assign.html, iframe-loading-lazy-nav-location-replace.html, iframe-loading-lazy-reload-location-reload.html and navigating-across-documents/005.html: 80/80 as expected. `./mach test-wpt --release --processes 2 html/semantics/forms/form-submission-0 html/semantics/embedded-content/the-iframe-element html/browsers/browsing-the-web/navigating-across-documents html/browsers/history html/browsers/browsing-the-web/overlapping-navigations-and-traversals` (506 tests): 500 as expected. Of the 6 others, replace-before-load/form-submit-cross-frame.html FAIL and location_replace_session_history.html CRASH happen as often on plain ohos-main (A/B: 10 repeats each and 3 runs of replace-before-load/), and cross-origin-top-navigation-with-user-activation-in-parent.window.html TIMEOUT, navigation-unload-same-origin-fragment.html FAIL, refresh/same-document-refresh.html PASS and jsurl-form-submit.tentative.html PASS were unexpected or flaky without the patch in the upstream A/B. Upstream (8de25a1ab6b) before and after: the form test hung in 5/25 and 6/25 runs, then 0/75; the new test 5/5 TIMEOUT, then 35/35 PASS. `./mach fmt` and `./mach test-tidy` are clean.
